                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e296b3f5-d010-4eab-8596-988487cdf692",
                        "source_entry_id": "b05d38cf-ccf8-32fa-aaea-adf072bc8904",
                        "source_sense_id": "e125b172-3880-3bee-98c2-61d82e532868",
                        "target_lang_word": "vulgarize",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vulgarize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58930e42-f668-3481-8992-5460d766eb7b",
                                        "entry_id": "39e8c826-00ed-3eae-9ca9-c4fdc6ce0fef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make vulgar.",
                                            "To make commonplace, crass, lewd."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a94cd545-a3e5-445b-8b79-4dc180a9ee17",
                                                "sense_id": "58930e42-f668-3481-8992-5460d766eb7b",
                                                "text": "With much labor we got our things up the steps, and then, looking back, took one last long survey of that strange land, soon I fear to be vulgarized, the prey of hunter and prospector, but to each of us a dreamland of glamour and romance, a land where we had dared much, suffered much, and learned much - our land, as we shall ever fondly call it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74f34659-c83f-4693-a4cd-f815e81cefea",
                                                "sense_id": "58930e42-f668-3481-8992-5460d766eb7b",
                                                "text": "\"Yes,\" said Mr. Flushing. \"And in my opinion,\" he continued, \"the absence of population to which Hirst objects is precisely the significant touch. You must admit, Hirst, that a little Italian town even would vulgarise the whole scene, would detract from the vastness — the sense of elemental grandeur.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b4a96a3-0000-4380-9501-5f63c5767c12",
                                                "sense_id": "58930e42-f668-3481-8992-5460d766eb7b",
                                                "text": "Words only vulgarize love and blunt its edge."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa0922f2-76cf-394c-887c-e3d2c8253c38",
                                        "entry_id": "39e8c826-00ed-3eae-9ca9-c4fdc6ce0fef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make vulgar.",
                                            "To convert (religious rites) so as to use the vulgate (language of the commoners)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d903b7d-efc7-47c9-ad51-0e04d8087926",
                        "source_entry_id": "b05d38cf-ccf8-32fa-aaea-adf072bc8904",
                        "source_sense_id": "e125b172-3880-3bee-98c2-61d82e532868",
                        "target_lang_word": "vulgariser",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vulgariser",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc7fbbf4-d7cd-3820-ab48-110da79c42cc",
                                        "entry_id": "cbb122a2-32ef-3e03-94b6-491c19bf045a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mettre à la portée de toutes les intelligences des notions de science et d’art."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6db0f65-d699-4ae9-9b2d-cd59b950d93f",
                                                "sense_id": "dc7fbbf4-d7cd-3820-ab48-110da79c42cc",
                                                "text": "Le 25 novembre dernier est décédé, à Dergneau, M. Léopold Bruneau qui, depuis plus de 30 ans, vulgarisait l'apiculture raisonnée dans sa région. Ses funérailles ont eu lieu au milieu d'une grande affluence de monde ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae75d3cf-eaf4-49de-b341-04ccf26d4f0f",
                                                "sense_id": "dc7fbbf4-d7cd-3820-ab48-110da79c42cc",
                                                "text": "Quoi qu'il en soit, Koestler avait le talent rare de rendre claires les idées absconses. Vulgariser sans verser dans la vulgarité, rendre intelligible l'inintelligible, tel est le grand talent de cet essayiste […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6968bff2-c7da-43d2-84e5-1d56f8565e99",
                                                "sense_id": "dc7fbbf4-d7cd-3820-ab48-110da79c42cc",
                                                "text": "Or quand les grands médias abandonnent leur devoir d’expliquer, de vulgariser, d’essayer de comprendre une réalité qui leur échappe, ils alimentent la méfiance de millions d’électeurs face aux élites."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
